{#- Where a free reader reaches for the plan, drawn by the server (design.md §12, "A free
    reader meets the plan where they reach for it", 2026-10-09; board PlanUpgradeMoment).
    The same panel `fault.js`'s `upgrade` draws: the sentence, Start a plan greyed with
    "Payments open soon", See plans, and what still works under a hairline. Expects
    `upgrade_said` and, optionally, `upgrade_fact`. -#}
<div class="fault-panel fault-upgrade" role="status">
  <p class="fault-panel-said">{{ upgrade_said }}</p>
  <div class="fault-panel-row">
    <button type="button" class="fault-go" disabled>{{ t("fault.start-a-plan", "Start a plan") }}</button>
    <span class="fault-fact fault-soon"><svg class="fault-clock" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 2.25a5.75 5.75 0 1 0 0 11.5a5.75 5.75 0 1 0 0-11.5z"/><path d="M8 5v3.2l2 1.3"/></svg>{{ t("fault.payments-soon", "Payments open soon") }}</span>
    <a class="fault-see" href="/plans">{{ t("fault.see-plans", "See plans") }}</a>
  </div>
  {%- if upgrade_fact %}
  <p class="fault-panel-foot">{{ upgrade_fact }}</p>
  {%- endif %}
</div>
